      "explanation": "Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.",
      "remediation": "Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.",
      "code_snippet": "- Writers: `/c-level-agents:decide` and the Chief of Staff (post board-meeting Phase 5). Individual role agents never write decisions directly.\n- decision-logger, chief-of-staff, and board-meeting all use this layout. Their SKILL.md files link here rather than defining their own paths.\n\n**Migration:** earlier versions used `memory/board-meetings/` (decision-logger, board-meeting) and `~/.claude/decision-log.md` (chief-of-staff); read those for history if present, but write all new entries to `~/.claude/decisions/`.\n\n## Quick Reference\n",
